The experimental B3 backend normalizes native integer division and modulo, including eligible typed bodies and active universal definitions. It adds native Real types, exact bounded rational literals, real arithmetic and division, integer embedding, floor, and eligible actual prelude conversion definitions. Existing nonzero-divisor and fractional-conversion obligations are preserved; no arithmetic assumptions are added. Fresh Real library verification and focused acceptance remain pending. The checked B3 language additionally has bounded positive-width native bitvector sorts, canonical literals, typed primitive operations, and aggregate resource admission. Dafny bitvector normalization, rotations, and power remain pending.
